# Citation metadata for OncoTriage Agent, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# GitHub parses this file and renders the "Cite this repository" control from
# it; a file that fails schema validation renders nothing at all and says
# nothing about why, so validate after editing:
#
#     pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate -i CITATION.cff
#
# WHY THERE IS NO `license:` KEY. That key takes an SPDX identifier and only an
# SPDX identifier -- the CFF 1.2.0 schema enumerates 459 of them and admits no
# `LicenseRef-` form and no all-rights-reserved entry, so this project's terms
# cannot be named there. `license-url` is the field the schema provides for
# exactly that case ("only for non-standard licenses not included in the SPDX
# License List") and it points at LICENSE, which is the authority.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, so nobody adds it back by guessing: there is no
# `doi:` and no `preferred-citation:` because no DOI has been minted and no
# paper exists; no `date-released:` because this version carries no release tag
# to date; and no author `orcid:` because no tracked file in this repository
# records one, and a citation file is not the place to invent one. The author
# `email:` IS recorded, deliberately: LICENSE clause 2 requires prior written
# permission for every use beyond reading, and a permission request needs an
# address to go to.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: OncoTriage Agent
message: >-
  If you reference this software, please cite it as below. Reuse requires the
  prior written permission of the copyright holder; see LICENSE.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alsaffar
    given-names: Ramy
    email: ramyalsaffar@gmail.com
version: "2.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ramyalsaffar/OncoTriage-Agent"
abstract: >-
  OncoTriage Agent matches oncology patients, represented as Synthea FHIR
  bundles, to recruiting ClinicalTrials.gov trials. It runs a six-stage
  LangGraph pipeline over hybrid BM25 and dense-vector retrieval on Qdrant,
  with a large language model performing criterion-level eligibility
  evaluation. It is a research and engineering demonstration on synthetic
  patient data and is not for clinical use.
keywords:
  - clinical trials
  - oncology
  - patient matching
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - LangGraph
  - FHIR
license-url: "https://github.com/ramyalsaffar/OncoTriage-Agent/blob/main/LICENSE"
